alm is that it feels so generically hip. This location is nice and contemporary but doesn't have any New Orleans charm - could be a restaurant in any trendy city so doesn't feel overly special in that sense. Definitely worth trying out if you're in the area. I'm sure I'll be back!"},{"business_id":"2XmP7QMdeiGTtJou5BMosQ","review_id":"PbVqXVHNaf-HjF75tmi5dg","date":"2019-08-12T18:02:13","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9349653720855713,"text_excerpt":"Love the new location. I used to have to drive to the bywater to get satsuma. The space is nice and has a huge yard for outdoor eating. They had a great special smoked salmon scrambled eggs topped with herb cream cheese. Why didn't I think of that??! Definitely a fan of satsuma and happy to have a location uptown"},{"business_id":"2XmP7QMdeiGTtJou5BMosQ","review_id":"fAvUnZfBjR9WyqACAXKG-g","date":"2019-09-26T18:08:53","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9316788911819458,"text_excerpt":"I've been coming here lately. This is the newest location from Satsuma café. Nice and quiet, large space. It's good to have a meeting, or get some work done. I love the chocolate cookies and the green eggs and ham sandwich served on a bagel is pretty tasty."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
